From: meta-local <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sama7d65_curiosity: enable the 2D GPU

The SAMA7D65 carries a Vivante GC520UL 2D graphics core, described in
sama7d65.dtsi as gpu@e1480000 with its bus/core clocks and a 533 MHz GPU PLL
assignment already in place, but left status = "disabled". No board DTS in the
tree references &gpu, so the GPU is unavailable on every sama7d65 board -- the
same is true of the GFX2D node on sam9x7, so this appears to be a deliberate
opt-in-per-board convention rather than an oversight.

Enable it on the Curiosity board so the nano2D kernel driver can bind and
userspace (libm2d) can use the core for 2D blit, stretch-blit and blend
operations. Without this the driver has nothing to probe against.

Enabling it costs nothing when unused: the block stays gated until a driver
claims it.

Signed-off-by: meta-local <noreply@example.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/microchip/at91-sama7d65_curiosity.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/microchip/at91-sama7d65_curiosity.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/microchip/at91-sama7d65_curiosity.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/microchip/at91-sama7d65_curiosity.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/microchip/at91-sama7d65_curiosity.dts
@@ -703,6 +703,10 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };

+&gpu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &vddout25 {
 	vin-supply = <&vdd_3v3>;
 	status = "okay";
